<title>UK: UK new car sales in April detailed -- SMMT.</title>
<headline>UK new car sales in April detailed -- SMMT.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>British new car sales</p>
<p> April		     182,747 vs 162,618 -- up 12.3 pct</p>
<p> Year to date	    732,281 vs 693,667 -- up  5.5 pct</p>
<p>Total for month by marque, market share in pct vs year ago</p>
<p> Ford		34,066 (18.6 pct) vs  31,142 (19.2 pct)</p>
<p> General Motors  25,810 (14.1 pct) vs  24,686 (15.2 pct)</p>
<p> Rover Group     18,040  (9.9 pct) vs  16,665 (10.3 pct)</p>
<p> Renault	   14,204  (7.8 pct) vs  10,558  (6.5 pct)</p>
<p> Peugeot	   13,906  (7.6 pct) vs  13,171  (8.1 pct)</p>
<p> VW		  11,172  (6.1 pct) vs   8,581  (5.3 pct)</p>
<p> Fiat		 7,683  (4.2 pct) vs   6,747  (4.2 pct)</p>
<p> Nissan	     7,549  (4.1 pct) vs   7,761  (4.8 pct)</p>
<p> Toyota	     6,726  (3.9 pct) vs   5,471  (3.4 pct)</p>
<p> Citroen	    4,664  (2.6 pct) vs   4,498  (2.8 pct)</p>
<p>Total yr to date by marque, market share in pct vs year ago</p>
<p> Ford	     131,732 (18.0 pct) vs 142,077 (20.5 pct)</p>
<p> General Motors 102,339 (14.0 pct) vs 104,628 (15.1 pct)</p>
<p> Rover Group     72,904 (10.0 pct) vs  75,609 (10.9 pct)</p>
<p> Peugeot	   55,738  (7.6 pct) vs  53,265  (7.7 pct)</p>
<p> Renault	   54,813  (7.5 pct) vs  44,786  (6.5 pct)</p>
<p> VW		  39,054  (5.3 pct) vs  34,577  (5.0 pct)</p>
<p> Nissan	    30,620  (4.2 pct) vs  31,129  (4.5 pct)</p>
<p> Citroen	   31,030  (4.2 pct) vs  25,264  (3.6 pct)</p>
<p> Fiat		29,209  (4.0 pct) vs  27,289  (3.9 pct)</p>
<p> Toyota	    25,558  (3.5 pct) vs  19,996  (2.9 pct)</p>
<p>NOTE: Figures provided by the Society of Motor Manufacturers and Traders Ltd.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4365</p>
